&lt;p&gt;Refer to the LCD-related Standard Documentation Requirements article, located at the bottom of this policy under the Related Local Coverage Documents section for additional information regarding these requirements.&lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;Refer to the Supplier Manual for additional information on documentation requirements.&lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;Refer to the DME MAC web sites for additional bulletin articles and other publications related to this LCD.&lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;POLICY SPECIFIC DOCUMENTATION REQUIREMENTS&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;Items covered in this LCD have additional policy-specific requirements that must be met prior to Medicare reimbursement. &lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;Refer to the LCD-related Policy article, located at the bottom of this policy under the Related Local Coverage Documents section for additional information.&lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Miscellaneous&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Appendices&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;APPENDIX A:&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt; EPWORTH SLEEPINESS SCALE&lt;&sol;u&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;How likely are you to doze off or fall asleep in the following situations, in contrast to feeling just tired? This refers to your usual way of life in recent times. Even if you have not done some of these things recently try to work out how they would have affected you.&lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;Use the following scale to choose the most appropriate number for each situation:&lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;0 = would never doze or sleep.&lt;br &sol;&gt;1 = slight chance of dozing or sleeping&lt;br &sol;&gt;2 = moderate chance of dozing or sleeping&lt;br &sol;&gt;3 = high chance of dozing or sleeping&lt;&sol;p&gt;
